{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/colinhacks/zod/pulls/6527","id":4404517719,"node_id":"PR_kwDODqUnoM8AAAABBoebVw","html_url":"https://github.com/colinhacks/zod/pull/6527","diff_url":"https://github.com/colinhacks/zod/pull/6527.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/colinhacks/zod/pull/6527.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/colinhacks/zod/issues/6527","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/colinhacks/zod/pulls/6527/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/colinhacks/zod/pulls/6527/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/colinhacks/zod/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/colinhacks/zod/issues/6527/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/colinhacks/zod/statuses/cbeac9415dc218eae98eaebc35971c0b6743528b","number":6527,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Emit a length-aware base64url pattern in toJSONSchema","user":{"login":"colinhacks","id":3084745,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwODQ3NDU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3084745?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/colinhacks","html_url":"https://github.com/colinhacks","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colinhacks/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colinhacks/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colinhacks/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colinhacks/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colinhacks/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colinhacks/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colinhacks/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colinhacks/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colinhacks/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #6516.\n\nz.base64url() rejects strings whose length is 1 (mod 4) — no encoder can produce them — but `def.pattern` held the charset-only regex, so `toJSONSchema()` emitted a pattern that accepts input parse rejects (`\"A\"`, `\"AAAAA\"`). This gives base64url the same split base64 already has: `regexes.base64url` is now the strict form and lands in the emitted schema, while `isValidBase64URL()` keeps a flat charset test — the quantified form overflows the regex stack on multi-MB input (the existing 10 MB test catches this), and the length rule is already enforced when the padded string reaches `isValidBase64()`. Parse behavior is unchanged; the compiled path reuses `isValidBase64URL()` and needs no change.\n\nOn the three axes: runtime is unchanged (the executed charset regex is identical; interleaved parse bench deltas sat inside same-revision spread), retained memory per schema is unchanged (~2,305 B both revisions), and bundle grows only for base64url users — classic full +52 B raw / +16 B gz, mini with base64url +56 B raw / +21 B gz, mini without it byte-identical.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-08-31T17:03:38Z","updated_at":"2026-08-31T17:16:16Z","closed_at":"2026-08-31T17:16:14Z","merged_at":"2026-08-31T17:16:14Z","merge_commit_sha":"319f47f44f40755773a9aa83b6fdaaad1ff01d77","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"colinhacks:fix-6516-base64url-pattern","ref":"fix-6516-base64url-pattern","repo":{"id":245704608,"node_id":"MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnkyNDU3MDQ2MDg=","name":"zod","full_name":"colinhacks/zod","owner":{"login":"colinhacks","id":3084745,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwODQ3NDU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3084745?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/colinhacks","html_url":"https://github.com/colinhacks","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colinhacks/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colinhacks/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colinhacks/gists{/gist